(Bugs #126/#127: refusing a malformed precision after a width - `{n:8.}`,
 `{n:8.2z}` - must not touch the WELL-formed pair right beside it. `{n:8.2}`
 and `{n:08.2}` still read both halves and keep both: the precision decides
 the digits, the width decides the padding (docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #85).)

a number called n is 255.
Print "[{n:8.2}]".
Print "[{n:08.2}]".
